{"type":"standard","title":"Sudovian language","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Sudovian language</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q35603","titles":{"canonical":"Sudovian_language","normalized":"Sudovian language","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Sudovian language</span></span>"},"pageid":42245,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/West_Baltic_languages.svg/330px-West_Baltic_languages.svg.png","width":330,"height":359},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/West_Baltic_languages.svg/1280px-West_Baltic_languages.svg.png","width":1000,"height":1088},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1353473386","tid":"9e8d28ae-4c79-11f1-b379-1f060b40d57d","timestamp":"2026-05-10T14:07:46Z","description":"Extinct Western Baltic language","description_source":"local","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudovian_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudovian_language?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudovian_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Sudovian_language"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudovian_language","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Sudovian_language","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sudovian_language?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Sudovian_language"}},"extract":"Sudovian was a West Baltic language of Northeastern Europe. Sudovian was closely related to Old Prussian. It was formerly spoken southwest of the Neman river in what is now Lithuania, east of Galindia and in the north of Yotvingia, and by exiles in East Prussia.","extract_html":"<p><b>Sudovian</b> was a West Baltic language of Northeastern Europe. Sudovian was closely related to Old Prussian. It was formerly spoken southwest of the Neman river in what is now Lithuania, east of Galindia and in the north of Yotvingia, and by exiles in East Prussia.</p>"}